# Responsive layout

Every screen works at a narrow phone width, a tablet width, and a desktop width.

- The page itself does not scroll sideways. A wide table or chart scrolls inside its own region.
- Navigation collapses on small screens. The product currently has a simple shell, so a new primary destination needs a small-screen path.
- Respect safe-area insets on fixed bars and sheets.
- Touch actions are available without hover. Tooltips repeat information that matters.
- Type and charts reflow. A modal that fits a desktop viewport becomes a sheet when the viewport is short.
- Verify at 320px and 768px, not only at the desktop default.

Detail is in `docs/quality/responsive-design.md`.
